unzip: a Unix entry with the PKWARE verification bit gets a default mode (homescoop#1401).
Debian's 04 keeps only the low byte of the external attributes when
internal attribute bit 2 is set, since the upper bytes then hold a
checksum. For a Unix-made entry that left mode 0, so the file was
extracted unreadable. The upper bytes are not a mode, so mapattr() now
takes the DOS branch for such an entry: 0666 (0444 with the read-only
bit, 0777 for a directory) less the umask, never a stored file type or
setuid bit.

--- a/unix/unix.c
+++ b/unix/unix.c
@@ -378,6 +378,8 @@
         case TANDEM_:
             r = FALSE;
             G.pInfo->file_attr = (unsigned)(tmp >> 16);
+            if (G.crec.internal_file_attributes & 0x0004)
+                r = TRUE;
             if (G.pInfo->file_attr == 0 && G.extra_field) {
                 /* Some (non-Info-ZIP) implementations of Zip for Unix and
                  * VMS (and probably others ??) leave 0 in the upper 16-bit
